<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alaska</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alaska is a large region in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. It was colonised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> from the eighteenth century, mainly for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a>, and administered through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-american-company">Russian-American Company</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> sold it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1867.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alaska.jpg" alt="Alaska" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benny Benson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Alaska.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
